            "name": "Elizabeth Slagle",
            "startSeconds": 197,
            "endSeconds": 412,
            "summary": "A 4th grade parent at Adelante Selby expressed concern about potential budget cuts including loss of a full-time teacher, possible class size increases from 22 to 31 students, and the impact these changes would have on vulnerable learners, urging the board to prioritize keeping current teachers and smaller class sizes."
          }
        ],
        "consent": false,
        "pulled": false
      },
      {
        "itemLabel": "9",
        "title": "Parcel Tax Discussion for November 2024 Ballot",
        "phases": {
          "opened": 456,
          "presentation": 546,
          "publicComment": 2841,
          "discussion": 1575,
          "vote": null
        },
        "publicComments": [
          {
            "name": "Jessica Shade",
            "startSeconds": 2858,
            "endSeconds": 2958,
            "summary": "A parent of two students at Orion voiced support for the parcel tax, noting that COVID stimulus funds which supported mental health counselors, reading specialists, and other services are ending and a parcel tax is critical to fill that gap."
          },
          {
            "name": "Brandon Matthews",
            "startSeconds": 2979,
            "endSeconds": 3002,
            "summary": "A homeowner and kindergarten parent at Adelante Selby voiced support for progressing as quickly as possible toward a parcel tax to support the schools."
          },
          {
            "name": "Elizabeth Slagle",
            "startSeconds": 3025,
            "endSeconds": 3113,
            "summary": "Having served on the prior Measure H campaign, she expressed support for the feasibility study while asking the board to examine lessons learned from that failed measure, particularly regarding online trolling that may have swayed voters, and also flagged a technical issue with the virtual speaker card website requiring a login."
          }
        ],
        "consent": false,
        "pulled": false
